{%- comment -%}
  Hyper's stylesheet only. Its theme.js is deliberately NOT loaded: every custom
  element it defines (basic-modal, drawer-component, accordion-details, product-form
  and 28 others) is already defined by this theme, so loading both throws
  "Identifier 'QuantityInput' has already been declared" and kills the rest of the
  script. This theme's own JS hydrates the markup instead.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'col-vendor.css' | asset_url }}" media="all">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'col-theme.css' | asset_url }}" media="all">
{%- comment -%}
  Hypers theme settings variables (:root and .color-scheme-*), scoped to .col-scope.
  Unscoped they would redefine 14 properties this theme also uses -- --color-background,
  --color-button and friends -- and recolour the header and footer on this page.
  Its @font-face rules are re-declared below against local copies of the fonts.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'col-vars.css' | asset_url }}" media="all">

{%- comment -%} col-fonts {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Poppins, the source page's typeface, self-hosted from this theme's assets rather
  than the source store's CDN. Declared here instead of in col-vars.css because the
  src needs asset_url, which a static .css file cannot use.

  The family is applied only inside .col-scope. Applied globally it would restyle
  this page's header, footer and cart drawer, which belong to this theme.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
@font-face{font-family:Poppins;font-weight:500;font-style:normal;font-display:swap;src:url({{ 'col-poppins-n5.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2"),url({{ 'col-poppins-n5.woff' | asset_url }}) format("woff");}
@font-face{font-family:Poppins;font-weight:500;font-style:italic;font-display:swap;src:url({{ 'col-poppins-i5.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2"),url({{ 'col-poppins-i5.woff' | asset_url }}) format("woff");}
@font-face{font-family:Poppins;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-display:swap;src:url({{ 'col-poppins-n7.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2"),url({{ 'col-poppins-n7.woff' | asset_url }}) format("woff");}
@font-face{font-family:Poppins;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-display:swap;src:url({{ 'col-poppins-i7.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2"),url({{ 'col-poppins-i7.woff' | asset_url }}) format("woff");}
@font-face{font-family:Poppins;font-weight:600;font-style:normal;font-display:swap;src:url({{ 'col-poppins-n6.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2"),url({{ 'col-poppins-n6.woff' | asset_url }}) format("woff");}
.col-scope, .col-scope *:not(svg):not(svg *){font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;}
/* Scoping the source stylesheet rewrote its html{} and body{} rules to
   ".col-scope html" and ".col-scope body" -- selectors that can never match -- so
   everything they declared was silently lost. That is why the page inherited this
   theme's 400/28.8px instead of the reference's 500/26px. The full set is re-seated
   on the scope root here. A prefixing pass is safe for class and :root selectors and
   destructive for html and body ones. */
.col-scope{font-family:var(--font-body-family);font-style:var(--font-body-style);font-weight:var(--font-body-weight,500);font-size:var(--font-body-size);line-height:var(--font-body-line-height,1.625);color:rgb(var(--color-foreground));-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale;font-feature-settings:normal;box-sizing:border-box;}
.col-scope *,.col-scope *::before,.col-scope *::after{box-sizing:border-box;}
</style>

{%- comment -%}
  The reference store runs no bundle app, so its buy box is subscription options, a
  quantity stepper, Add To Cart and Buy with Shop. Kaching Bundles injects its tier
  block here through a store-wide app embed -- there is no theme markup to remove --
  so it is hidden with CSS scoped to .col-scope. Only this landing page is affected;
  NAC, Selerb and magnesium keep their bundle offers.

  kaching-bundles.js hides .product-form__quantity whenever tiers drive quantity, so
  with the tiers gone the stepper has to be given back explicitly.

  kaching-subscriptions is a separate embed, deliberately left alone -- it renders the
  subscribe/one-time options the reference also shows.
  NOTE the selectors below are exact class tokens, not a [class*="kaching-bundles"]
  wildcard. Kaching stamps "kaching-bundles-form--different" onto the product form
  itself, so the wildcard matched the form and hid the buy button with it -- the page
  looked right and silently could not add to cart. Only the tier UI is hidden here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
.col-scope kaching-bundle,
.col-scope .kaching-bundles{display:none !important;}
.col-scope .product-form__quantity{display:block !important;}
</style>

{%- comment -%}
  Class-name collisions. This theme ships its own image-with-text and multicolumn
  sections using the same BEM names as the source theme, and its base.css styles the
  ported markup as if it were its own:

    .image-with-text__content { display:flex; padding: 6rem 7rem 7rem; }
    .multicolumn-card__info   { padding: 2.5rem; }

  The 7rem inset is what squeezed the image-with-text heading to 375px instead of the
  reference's 515px, wrapping it onto a third line; the 2.5rem one narrowed the
  multicolumn text from 413px to 363px. Both are reset to what the reference computes.
  Scoped to .col-scope, so this theme's own sections are untouched.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
.col-scope .image-with-text__content{display:block;padding:0;}
.col-scope .multicolumn-card__info{padding:0;}
</style>
